    <note type="translation" xml:lang="en">Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Badr, al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī, the merchant. A resident of Mecca and father of Muḥammad, and brother of Muḥammad (mentioned below). He was known as al-Jaʿjāʿ. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca.</note>
